WEBVTT

00:42.542 --> 00:45.962
SOLD OUT ON YOU

00:51.050 --> 00:52.010
Good night.

00:53.011 --> 00:54.137
All right.

00:54.220 --> 00:55.221
You too.

01:01.978 --> 01:03.271
-I…
-Hey…

01:06.524 --> 01:07.400
Go first.

01:09.360 --> 01:10.570
Well…

01:11.279 --> 01:14.491
I don't think
I'll be able to sleep easily tonight.

01:15.116 --> 01:16.951
Why don't we talk about

01:17.035 --> 01:20.663
something really boring
that would make anyone fall asleep?

01:22.248 --> 01:24.626
We can talk about
that poetry book from last time too.

01:28.171 --> 01:30.548
I guess we shouldn't ruin
our whole day tomorrow…

01:30.632 --> 01:31.633
No, I mean…

01:32.634 --> 01:33.718
It's only one day, so…

01:35.595 --> 01:39.057
I just thought of the perfect book.
It'll be hard for you to understand it.

01:40.058 --> 01:41.059
Come with me.

01:42.268 --> 01:43.269
What is it?

01:43.770 --> 01:47.774
HIDDEN ORDER OF THE PHYSICAL WORLD

01:47.857 --> 01:50.860
So this is the kind of book you read.

01:55.198 --> 01:58.284
Mr. Seo seemed like he wanted
to talk to you earlier.

01:58.368 --> 01:59.953
What did you talk about?

02:01.037 --> 02:03.540
Why are you suddenly bringing up Mr. Seo?

02:03.623 --> 02:04.707
I'm just curious.

02:05.208 --> 02:06.626
Am I not allowed to ask?

02:07.794 --> 02:09.712
We talked about work.

02:09.796 --> 02:11.005
Work?

02:14.092 --> 02:15.176
All right.

02:15.718 --> 02:18.138
This book explains
different types of chemical bonds.

02:18.221 --> 02:21.891
Ionic compounds and molecular compounds
are especially important.

02:21.975 --> 02:22.809
Right, ionic…

02:22.892 --> 02:24.227
Like ions in sports drinks?

02:24.310 --> 02:25.145
Yes.

02:25.645 --> 02:28.148
First, you need to know
the definition of ionic compounds.

02:59.387 --> 03:00.305
Yes, Dad.

03:01.222 --> 03:02.223
I'm with Eric.

03:03.349 --> 03:05.518
I'll take care of everything. Don't worry.

03:07.812 --> 03:09.689
Don't push him too hard, all right?

03:10.481 --> 03:12.317
All right. Bye.

03:13.818 --> 03:14.903
Hey, little brother.

03:17.655 --> 03:19.157
What is this?

03:20.074 --> 03:21.826
You two looked good together.

03:21.910 --> 03:22.744
What?

03:22.827 --> 03:27.040
I want you to laugh and smile
without any worries,

03:27.624 --> 03:30.543
just like you were doing in that photo.

03:31.628 --> 03:33.463
You've put in so much work.

03:33.546 --> 03:35.298
I'll take care of everything now,

03:35.381 --> 03:37.717
so just listen to your favorite music
and get some rest.

03:45.558 --> 03:46.392
Michelle.

03:47.060 --> 03:49.187
There's one thing
you need to do before that.

03:49.687 --> 03:51.189
What was their name again?

03:52.065 --> 03:54.067
-HIT.
-Right, HIT.

03:54.651 --> 03:58.571
Go and tell them you've changed your mind
and you don't want to do the broadcast.

03:58.655 --> 04:01.366
I'm in charge of the Korea launch.
I'll handle it on my own.

04:07.205 --> 04:08.039
Eric.

04:10.541 --> 04:13.378
Remember the tale
"The Frog and the Ox" that we read as kids

04:14.003 --> 04:16.005
from La Fontaine's Fables?

04:17.090 --> 04:20.927
The frog kept puffing itself up
to become as big as the ox.

04:21.469 --> 04:23.221
And what happened in the end?

04:26.015 --> 04:28.434
Boom. It exploded and died.

04:31.813 --> 04:34.315
It should've just kept living
the way it used to.

04:34.899 --> 04:36.359
Don't you think?

04:42.031 --> 04:44.158
How is the factory manager?

04:44.242 --> 04:47.328
Yes, ma'am. He's a fearful man,
so I'm sure he'll keep quiet.

04:47.412 --> 04:49.330
We paid him a handsome amount as well.

04:49.414 --> 04:53.209
As soon as things are wrapped up with HIT,
get rid of all the essence there.

04:53.293 --> 04:54.419
Yes, ma'am.

05:12.478 --> 05:14.147
Mr. Park, what are you doing here?

05:14.230 --> 05:15.315
Geez, you scared me!

05:18.359 --> 05:22.196
Geez, you were trying to squeeze money
out of Mechoori again, weren't you?

05:22.280 --> 05:23.406
No, I wasn't.

05:23.489 --> 05:26.326
Then, what about you?
Why were you looking for Ms. Dam?

05:27.327 --> 05:28.703
Do you like her?

05:28.786 --> 05:30.997
No, I like Ms. Eom…

05:31.622 --> 05:33.041
Geez.

05:33.541 --> 05:36.544
What would a kid know?
Just hurry up and go to school.

05:36.627 --> 05:39.380
-I can do what I want.
-Well, I can do what I want too.

05:39.464 --> 05:40.548
Fine. Don't go then.

05:40.631 --> 05:41.966
You can't do that either.

05:42.050 --> 05:45.511
You're not letting me do anything.
What's your deal?

05:45.595 --> 05:48.264
It's because you keep saying
things I can't allow.

05:48.347 --> 05:49.390
Are they fighting?

05:49.474 --> 05:50.808
I want to go to the farm too.

05:50.892 --> 05:52.560
Just rest until your ankle's better.

05:52.643 --> 05:54.771
-I want to be with you.
-No.

05:54.854 --> 05:56.647
There you go saying no again.

05:57.440 --> 05:59.525
-Let's make a bet.
-A bet?

05:59.609 --> 06:02.570
If I win,
you can only say "yes" from now on.

06:02.653 --> 06:05.281
But if I lose, I won't complain anymore.
What do you say?

06:05.364 --> 06:07.283
-All right.
-All right!

06:09.160 --> 06:11.329
Okay. I'll hide this in one of my hands,

06:11.412 --> 06:12.997
and you have to guess where it is.

06:16.167 --> 06:17.043
Don't look.

06:17.126 --> 06:18.377
Come on, turn around.

06:20.880 --> 06:22.507
All right.

06:23.758 --> 06:24.967
Guess where it is!

06:33.643 --> 06:35.812
Right? Left?

06:35.895 --> 06:38.022
Left? Right?

06:39.148 --> 06:40.149
Right!

06:40.733 --> 06:42.110
Wrong!

06:42.193 --> 06:43.945
It's not there! Yes!

06:44.028 --> 06:46.656
I won, so you have to say yes
to everything from now on. Okay?

06:46.739 --> 06:47.782
What sort of game…

06:51.202 --> 06:52.036
All right.

06:52.620 --> 06:55.748
Then, can I come with you
to the farm today?

06:59.418 --> 07:01.420
-Fine. Yes.
-Great.

07:02.421 --> 07:04.423
-Let's go.
-Wait…

07:05.591 --> 07:07.301
We're walking to the farm like this?

07:12.598 --> 07:15.351
Then, just until over there.

07:15.435 --> 07:16.811
Okay?

07:19.188 --> 07:20.106
Okay.

07:34.787 --> 07:37.957
Why are you covering my eyes?
They didn't even do anything.

07:38.040 --> 07:39.459
You little…

07:41.127 --> 07:42.962
They can't get enough of each other!

07:43.045 --> 07:44.297
Why are you so upset?

07:44.380 --> 07:47.091
Mechoori needs to end up with Jin-yi.

07:48.217 --> 07:49.427
Forget it.

07:49.510 --> 07:50.595
Where are you going?

07:50.678 --> 07:52.930
School. Where else would I be going?

07:53.014 --> 07:55.808
You said you weren't going.
How ridiculous.

07:57.185 --> 07:59.353
-Hey, Mechoori.
-Hey.

07:59.437 --> 08:01.439
Ms. Dam is here too!

08:01.522 --> 08:02.899
-Hello.
-You're all here early.

08:02.982 --> 08:04.192
-It's good to see you.
-Oh, my.

08:04.275 --> 08:06.736
Ms. Dam's face is practically glowing.

08:06.819 --> 08:07.653
It is.

08:07.737 --> 08:10.573
Mechoori's face looks even brighter.

08:10.656 --> 08:14.952
How can he look so happy
after ruining the festival yesterday?

08:17.622 --> 08:19.123
What did you two do last night?

08:25.838 --> 08:27.006
Focus on work, everyone.

08:27.089 --> 08:28.424
Gosh, how embarrassing.

08:28.508 --> 08:31.010
I mean, it can happen.
They're adults. It's no big deal.

08:32.553 --> 08:34.180
That's enough. Let's get back to work.

08:35.765 --> 08:38.226
Hey, Kwang-mo. Why are you so late?

08:38.309 --> 08:39.519
You should be on time.

08:39.602 --> 08:40.645
Something came up.

08:43.439 --> 08:44.690
Hey, Mechoori.

08:46.359 --> 08:47.652
What's with that look?

08:48.611 --> 08:49.445
What?

08:50.196 --> 08:51.280
It's nothing.

08:51.364 --> 08:52.198
All right.

08:52.281 --> 08:57.245
Everyone, please do your best
today as well!

08:57.828 --> 08:59.872
With all your love and care!

08:59.956 --> 09:02.458
Okay, let's go!

09:02.542 --> 09:04.043
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

09:04.126 --> 09:06.546
Yes. You just need to check that.

09:07.421 --> 09:08.631
All right, bye.

09:16.389 --> 09:17.807
Could you scooch over a bit?

09:17.890 --> 09:18.808
Let me turn this off.

09:37.493 --> 09:38.619
Born and raised in Deokpung,

09:38.703 --> 09:41.247
I'm Park Kwang-mo,
and I'm here today to introduce

09:41.330 --> 09:42.415
a wild boar repellent.

09:42.498 --> 09:44.250
Do wild boar repellents exist?

09:44.333 --> 09:45.376
Oh, my gosh.

09:45.459 --> 09:46.794
What on earth?

09:46.877 --> 09:48.629
Geez, that startled me.

09:48.713 --> 09:51.340
Our broadcast begins in ten minutes.

09:54.051 --> 09:55.678
Mr. Park!

10:02.643 --> 10:04.937
Jung-muk!

10:05.980 --> 10:06.939
Jung-muk!

10:07.023 --> 10:09.942
Jung-muk, look at this.
What do you think this means?

10:10.776 --> 10:12.403
Oh, right. So this person is… Well…

10:12.486 --> 10:13.529
The arm wrestler.

10:13.613 --> 10:15.031
You remember her, right?

10:15.114 --> 10:16.407
Anyway,

10:16.490 --> 10:19.327
Ms. Eom just sent me a selfie,

10:19.410 --> 10:21.495
saying her broadcast
starts in ten minutes.

10:21.579 --> 10:23.998
What does it mean?
Why did she send that? For what reason?

10:25.666 --> 10:27.251
She's asking you to buy their stuff.

10:28.002 --> 10:29.128
To increase their sales.

10:29.879 --> 10:30.713
Is that so?

10:30.796 --> 10:31.672
Yeah.

10:36.844 --> 10:38.804
Connect to an agent.

10:39.513 --> 10:41.766
Delivered to your door with care.
HIT Homeshopping.

10:41.849 --> 10:44.435
I'd like the products
that Producer Eom Sung-mi is selling.

10:44.518 --> 10:46.145
You know,

10:46.228 --> 10:48.856
the organic goat milk baby formula
from Kilimanjaro.

10:48.939 --> 10:50.775
Yes, that's the one!

10:50.858 --> 10:54.070
I'd like about ten of those
in the highest grade.

10:54.820 --> 10:55.821
Okay, bye!

10:56.906 --> 10:58.115
ORDER DETAILS

10:58.199 --> 11:00.326
Hey, you're good
at speaking standard Korean.

11:00.409 --> 11:02.662
Pretty good, right?
You can do it with practice too.

11:02.745 --> 11:05.081
"I bought them."

11:05.164 --> 11:07.833
Jung-muk, I would've made
a huge mistake if it weren't for you.

11:07.917 --> 11:09.543
-Right?
-Thanks.

11:09.627 --> 11:10.544
-Bye, then.
-Bye.

11:23.516 --> 11:25.518
Should we get going too?

11:26.519 --> 11:28.729
Why don't you go first?
I'll head out after I wrap up.

11:28.813 --> 11:29.772
Hey!

11:32.983 --> 11:34.902
How long are you going to do that for?

11:38.114 --> 11:39.323
About a week?

11:40.074 --> 11:42.910
Fine. I'll go easy on you.
I'll do it just for today.

11:43.702 --> 11:44.537
All right.

11:45.246 --> 11:47.665
But can I plan the course
for our morning run tomorrow?

11:49.375 --> 11:50.793
-Sure.
-No, wait.

11:50.876 --> 11:52.628
Why don't we just take the day off?

11:53.170 --> 11:55.381
-All right.
-No, wait.

11:55.464 --> 11:57.842
Let's just skip running
this evening too while we're at it.

11:57.925 --> 11:59.760
Let's take a proper break this time.

12:01.470 --> 12:02.555
Okay, fine.

12:04.056 --> 12:05.057
Mr. Mechoori.

12:05.558 --> 12:08.394
Why don't we do a TV show marathon
after dinner today?

12:08.477 --> 12:10.563
There's something
I'd really wanted to watch.

12:11.355 --> 12:12.273
Sure.

12:12.356 --> 12:15.359
An ordinary office worker goes
on a blind date in her friend's place,

12:15.443 --> 12:17.653
and she's asked to ruin the date.

12:17.736 --> 12:20.823
So she did all sorts
of ridiculous things in front of the guy,

12:20.906 --> 12:23.534
but he actually proposes to her.

12:23.617 --> 12:24.660
But the problem is

12:24.743 --> 12:27.830
he's the CEO of the company
that the female lead works for.

12:29.123 --> 12:31.667
I heard once you start watching,
you can't stop until the end.

12:31.750 --> 12:34.462
And the male lead looks a lot like you.

12:35.880 --> 12:37.256
Is that so?

12:38.007 --> 12:39.425
That seems fun in multiple aspects.

12:40.676 --> 12:44.054
-How many episodes are there?
-Twelve episodes.

12:45.598 --> 12:48.225
Are you suggesting we stay up all night?
We can't do that.

12:49.393 --> 12:52.730
But it won't be fun
if we stop in the middle.

12:52.813 --> 12:55.566
-You'll be watching it with me.
-What?

12:56.817 --> 12:58.319
You'll be watching it with me.

13:08.704 --> 13:09.914
I'm so thirsty!

13:09.997 --> 13:12.416
You must be thirsty too
after working for so long.

13:13.209 --> 13:15.419
I'll go get something to drink.

13:24.220 --> 13:28.057
Gosh, what's gotten into him?
He must be crazy. I was so startled.

13:29.767 --> 13:31.810
"If I become class president…"

13:31.894 --> 13:35.648
"If I become class president,
I'll go up to those who feel left out…"

13:35.731 --> 13:38.859
-Som-yi?
-"…and I'll talk to them first."

13:38.943 --> 13:42.530
"I'm not good with words,
but I'll stay by their side--"

13:42.613 --> 13:44.365
No, you should say you're good.

13:44.907 --> 13:45.741
What are you doing?

13:46.325 --> 13:47.868
What are you practicing?

13:47.952 --> 13:49.495
You're running for class president?

13:49.578 --> 13:51.205
Will you please be quiet?

13:51.288 --> 13:52.623
Why?

13:52.706 --> 13:53.791
Is it a secret?

13:54.458 --> 13:56.544
I'm sure I won't get elected anyway.

13:56.627 --> 13:59.004
Come on. You can't be sure
when you haven't even tried.

13:59.088 --> 14:03.092
The other kids won't even know my name
because I'm always wearing a mask.

14:04.760 --> 14:07.263
But there's a reason
why you want to do it, right?

14:08.097 --> 14:12.851
If I become class president,
I can be friends with everyone.

14:19.608 --> 14:21.986
Then, let's do it!

14:22.069 --> 14:23.862
How could I ever become class president?

14:23.946 --> 14:25.948
I'm Dam Ye-jin, you know.

14:26.031 --> 14:29.243
I can bring in 100 million won a minute
as soon as I start talking.

14:29.785 --> 14:32.872
Want me to show you
how to use your speech to captivate

14:32.955 --> 14:34.748
the entire class in three minutes?

14:34.832 --> 14:37.334
Then, will I really
be able to become class president?

14:37.418 --> 14:39.420
Of course. Follow me.

14:41.672 --> 14:43.507
This is your first lesson.

14:43.591 --> 14:45.801
You need a campaign promise
that will captivate them.

14:45.885 --> 14:48.804
You need something that can easily show
what kind of person you are

14:48.888 --> 14:50.973
and what kind of president you want to be.

14:53.809 --> 14:56.812
"Everyone will be included…"

14:57.354 --> 14:58.689
To gain more votes,

14:58.772 --> 15:00.983
it would be nice
to promise snacks as well.

15:01.066 --> 15:03.485
I want to be a president
with a generous heart,

15:03.569 --> 15:05.195
not a generous wallet.

15:07.364 --> 15:08.741
NA SOM-YI

15:08.824 --> 15:09.783
I'd pick you.

15:09.867 --> 15:11.410
You should be the next village chief.

15:13.120 --> 15:14.204
Here's the second lesson.

15:14.830 --> 15:17.499
You need a killer smile with your eyes.

15:17.583 --> 15:20.127
Do you think wearing a mask
hides all your expressions?

15:20.210 --> 15:22.630
No, you can just speak
with your eyes. Like this.

15:22.713 --> 15:24.840
Lift your cheekbones as high as you can,

15:24.924 --> 15:26.926
and let the outer corners
of your eyes tilt down.

15:29.261 --> 15:31.931
No, not like that. Let's try it once more.

15:34.934 --> 15:36.685
Is this right?

15:37.353 --> 15:38.562
Well…

15:38.646 --> 15:40.856
Why don't we try
relaxing your facial muscles first?

15:40.940 --> 15:42.399
Repeat after me.

15:42.483 --> 15:46.111
A, E, I, O, U.

15:46.987 --> 15:49.073
A, E, I…

15:49.740 --> 15:52.493
It's finally our third lesson!
Vocal training.

15:52.576 --> 15:56.288
I'll teach you how to speak
loud and clearly even with a mask on.

15:56.872 --> 15:59.833
All right, take a deep breath.

16:01.627 --> 16:04.838
Do you feel your throat opening?
Inhale deeply.

16:04.922 --> 16:07.424
Then, when you feel like
your stomach's filled with air…

16:07.925 --> 16:10.260
-This is too hard.
-Really?

16:13.389 --> 16:15.099
Are there any K-pop idols you like?

16:15.182 --> 16:17.184
Ji-nu from Lion Boys.

16:17.267 --> 16:21.438
Okay, imagine that Ji-nu from Lion Boys
is standing way over there

16:21.522 --> 16:23.357
and you're calling out to him.

16:23.941 --> 16:25.484
Ji-nu!

16:25.567 --> 16:27.861
-Louder!
-Ji-nu!

16:34.368 --> 16:35.244
Here's my number.

16:38.831 --> 16:41.417
If you get stuck on anything,
you can call me anytime.

16:41.500 --> 16:43.002
Yes, Coach.

16:43.085 --> 16:46.255
I guess home shopping hosts
are really skilled at stuff like this.

16:47.339 --> 16:50.342
I think my sister
would be great at it too.

16:51.010 --> 16:55.097
Her dream was actually
to become a home shopping host.

16:56.056 --> 16:59.393
But she's running the shop here
because of me.

17:00.352 --> 17:03.272
HIT is looking for
new hosts to hire right now.

17:04.189 --> 17:05.816
You could suggest it to her.

17:05.899 --> 17:08.360
I think Jin-yi would do pretty well.

17:10.571 --> 17:12.197
Jin-yi!

17:12.990 --> 17:15.701
-Jin-yi, look at this.
-What is it?

17:15.784 --> 17:17.411
Can't you try out for this, Jin-yi?

17:17.494 --> 17:19.496
Ms. Dam said she thinks you'd do well.

17:19.580 --> 17:21.874
Dam Ye-jin? You were with her just now?

17:21.957 --> 17:24.376
I just ran into her.

17:24.460 --> 17:27.379
Anyway, can't you try applying
to be a home shopping host?

17:27.463 --> 17:29.214
Can't you?

17:29.298 --> 17:31.800
-Come on. Please.
-That's enough.

17:32.468 --> 17:33.677
Go and wash up for dinner.

17:37.306 --> 17:38.932
Just think about it, okay?

17:45.230 --> 17:46.607
SOMSOM

17:46.690 --> 17:49.151
HIT HOMESHOPPING
OPEN RECRUITMENT FOR HOSTS

17:57.159 --> 17:58.243
I'm back.

17:59.620 --> 18:01.371
What took you so long?

18:01.955 --> 18:02.831
It's a secret.

18:12.257 --> 18:13.801
Now that I think about it,

18:13.884 --> 18:17.304
I think I first fell for you
when I saw you like this.

18:17.387 --> 18:19.014
It's when I saw you absorbed in work.

18:20.140 --> 18:24.436
The laser focus in your eyes
struck a chord within my soul.

18:25.521 --> 18:26.522
What?

18:27.356 --> 18:29.066
You talk to yourself too loudly.

18:29.149 --> 18:30.943
I said that for you to hear.

18:32.778 --> 18:36.740
But aren't you tired?
You've been working all day.

18:37.241 --> 18:38.325
I'm fine.

18:39.409 --> 18:40.410
I get it.

18:41.453 --> 18:44.998
When you're doing something you like,
you always wish for more time, not energy.

18:46.625 --> 18:50.629
It's wonderful when you have something
you're so passionate about.

18:51.922 --> 18:53.423
It makes you feel like you're alive.

19:00.973 --> 19:01.974
Do you want to try this?

19:03.725 --> 19:05.644
-Can I?
-Come here.

19:08.730 --> 19:09.565
Here.

19:10.524 --> 19:12.526
You're supposed to wear gloves…

19:13.402 --> 19:15.237
But today, you can just try it.

19:16.613 --> 19:17.614
This one?

19:18.657 --> 19:20.200
-Hold it closer to the tip.
-Okay.

19:20.284 --> 19:22.327
-Be careful. Hold the top a bit more.
-Be careful…

19:23.412 --> 19:24.913
Is this the right way?

19:24.997 --> 19:26.331
And I hold it here?

19:26.874 --> 19:28.959
This is so nerve-racking!

19:29.042 --> 19:31.545
Am I doing it right?

19:31.628 --> 19:33.213
Is this good?

19:33.297 --> 19:34.506
Mr. Mechoori…

20:08.290 --> 20:09.291
What do we do?

20:56.838 --> 20:57.839
Mr. Mechoori.

20:58.966 --> 21:00.884
The TV show was really fun, wasn't it?

21:01.385 --> 21:03.136
You have to watch it with me tomorrow too.

21:05.222 --> 21:06.056
All right.

21:08.267 --> 21:10.477
It must've been tough
saying yes to me all day.

21:11.520 --> 21:12.980
But I had fun thanks to you.

21:13.647 --> 21:14.731
You should get some sleep.

21:16.942 --> 21:18.151
Good night.

21:18.986 --> 21:19.987
Good night.

21:49.516 --> 21:52.894
Candidate Na Som-yi.
Do you feel a bit more confident now?

21:53.645 --> 21:56.648
I'm okay with everything else,

21:57.733 --> 21:59.359
but my mask…

22:00.694 --> 22:03.530
All right. Here's my final lesson.

22:04.573 --> 22:06.491
Do you see this mole here?

22:06.575 --> 22:08.452
Has it ever bothered you before though?

22:09.870 --> 22:12.331
It's the same with your mask.

22:12.414 --> 22:14.833
If it doesn't bother you,
it won't bother anyone else either.

22:14.916 --> 22:17.044
Come on. The sizes are different.

22:17.794 --> 22:20.339
My mask is clearly visible.

22:20.422 --> 22:21.256
Som-yi.

22:21.340 --> 22:24.301
What your classmates will see today
during the election

22:24.384 --> 22:27.763
is the sincerity from your heart,
not your appearance.

22:28.555 --> 22:29.973
The heart doesn't have eyes.

22:30.057 --> 22:31.892
Whether you wear a mask
or a magnifying glass,

22:31.975 --> 22:33.226
it won't matter at all.

22:35.437 --> 22:37.773
If appearances made you class president,

22:37.856 --> 22:41.276
I would've become president
a hundred times over, don't you think?

22:42.110 --> 22:42.944
Geez.

22:44.196 --> 22:46.531
I'm sure you got the message.
You're dismissed.

22:46.615 --> 22:47.824
Yes, Coach.

22:56.208 --> 22:58.960
I'll do my best as class president.

22:59.044 --> 23:00.378
Thank you.

23:00.879 --> 23:03.090
Next is the second candidate, Na Som-yi.

23:13.308 --> 23:15.727
CANDIDATE 1 SHIN DO-A
PIZZA PARTY, SNACKS, NEW BOARD GAMES

23:15.811 --> 23:18.605
CANDIDATE 2 NA SOM-YI
ALL INCLUSIVE, I'LL HELP, MESSAGE BOX

23:25.862 --> 23:27.948
Hello, everyone.

23:28.448 --> 23:31.159
I'm Candidate Number Two, Na Som-yi…

23:31.243 --> 23:33.078
-I can't hear her.
-Can you hear her?

23:33.161 --> 23:34.663
-What's she saying?
-I can't hear her.

23:34.746 --> 23:35.831
I can't hear anything.

23:35.914 --> 23:37.874
-What is she saying?
-I can't hear at all.

23:37.958 --> 23:39.584
-I can't hear anything.
-It's her mask.

23:41.628 --> 23:43.630
If it weren't for this mask…

23:44.214 --> 23:46.842
If it doesn't bother you,
it won't bother anyone else either.

23:46.925 --> 23:49.511
What your classmates will see today
during the election

23:49.594 --> 23:53.223
is the sincerity from your heart,
not your appearance.

23:54.891 --> 23:57.978
All right, take a deep breath.

23:58.061 --> 24:00.021
2025 CLASS PRESIDENT ELECTION

24:00.105 --> 24:02.482
Okay, imagine that Ji-nu from Lion Boys

24:02.566 --> 24:04.234
is standing way over there

24:04.317 --> 24:06.194
and you're calling out to him.

24:08.738 --> 24:10.782
I want to become class president

24:10.866 --> 24:15.078
because I don't want anyone
in our class to feel left out.

24:15.912 --> 24:18.957
To make sure
that everyone in our class is included,

24:19.040 --> 24:21.042
I will always rush over and help.

24:21.126 --> 24:22.544
I'll become a president

24:22.627 --> 24:26.131
who reaches out first
to anyone who feels left out.

24:26.214 --> 24:27.841
Thank you.

24:38.351 --> 24:39.561
CLASS PRESIDENT ELECTION

24:39.644 --> 24:42.606
SHIN DO-A, 7 VOTES
NA SOM-YI, 7 VOTES

24:42.689 --> 24:44.399
BALLOT BOX

24:48.320 --> 24:49.154
All right.

24:49.237 --> 24:52.073
Our new class president is…

24:56.244 --> 24:57.454
Na Som-yi!

25:03.627 --> 25:05.712
Hey, I thought you couldn't speak.

25:05.795 --> 25:07.589
-What?
-You were really cool.

25:08.340 --> 25:09.341
Thanks.

25:09.424 --> 25:11.384
Hey, want to hang out in town later?

25:11.468 --> 25:12.385
Join us.

25:12.469 --> 25:13.511
Okay?

25:13.595 --> 25:14.846
Me too. Let me join you.

25:14.930 --> 25:17.933
-Me too. Let me join you.
-Me too.

25:18.016 --> 25:20.143
-Let's go.
-Me too.

25:20.227 --> 25:22.270
-Me too.
-Come with us.

25:26.066 --> 25:27.067
Shin Do-a.

25:28.443 --> 25:29.819
Join us.

25:33.031 --> 25:34.866
Okay. Sure.

25:34.950 --> 25:37.577
-Yeah, let's all hang out together!
-Let's go!

25:37.661 --> 25:39.037
Just throw this in for me.

25:39.120 --> 25:42.415
Come on. I won't have anything left.
I'll go broke at this rate.

25:42.499 --> 25:43.750
Geez.

25:43.833 --> 25:45.335
But I'll deliver them to your houses.

25:45.961 --> 25:47.587
Do you need anything else?

25:52.217 --> 25:54.302
Jin-yi, I'm class president!

25:54.803 --> 25:56.137
Class president?

25:56.221 --> 25:58.431
Class president?
You ran for class president?

25:58.515 --> 25:59.349
Yeah.

25:59.432 --> 26:01.268
So I'm going to be a bit late today.

26:01.351 --> 26:03.270
I'm going to karaoke with my friends.

26:08.984 --> 26:11.194
Tell me if there's anything you need!

26:16.533 --> 26:17.367
Hello?

26:17.450 --> 26:19.869
Mechoori, why weren't you picking up?

26:19.953 --> 26:21.162
Hey, Som-yi.

26:21.705 --> 26:22.789
Sorry, I was working.

26:22.872 --> 26:24.666
I became class president.

26:25.250 --> 26:27.460
It's all thanks to Coach Dam Ye-jin.

26:27.544 --> 26:29.254
I wouldn't have made it without her.

26:29.337 --> 26:30.171
Som-yi, come on.

26:30.255 --> 26:32.590
-Hurry up.
-Hang on!

26:32.674 --> 26:33.883
Hurry up, Som-yi!

26:33.967 --> 26:35.468
My friends are calling me. Bye!

26:50.025 --> 26:51.401
Ms. Dam.

26:52.319 --> 26:53.153
Welcome home.

26:53.778 --> 26:55.864
Right. Mr. Mechoori,
did you hear the news?

26:55.947 --> 26:57.741
Som-yi got elected.

26:57.824 --> 27:00.035
I'm so proud of her.

27:00.118 --> 27:03.496
She was so worried
but did her speech confidently in class.

27:03.580 --> 27:06.583
The news made me happier
than when I would sell out.

27:06.666 --> 27:07.876
What were you doing?

27:09.294 --> 27:13.214
Well, after I saw you working yesterday,
I felt the itch to work again too.

27:13.298 --> 27:16.051
So I've been reviewing a list
of product offers I received.

27:18.470 --> 27:20.221
You'll be able to work again soon enough.

27:21.681 --> 27:24.100
The numbers still
haven't exceeded the limit yet?

27:26.186 --> 27:27.020
No.

27:28.438 --> 27:30.523
Right. That's actually good.

27:31.066 --> 27:33.902
I'm going to choose
my comeback product very carefully.

27:36.404 --> 27:37.697
DAD

27:39.741 --> 27:41.159
Hang on.

27:52.128 --> 27:53.880
-Hello?
-Hey, Ye-jin.

27:55.382 --> 27:57.592
You didn't seem to be
coming home these days.

27:57.675 --> 27:59.177
Did you go somewhere for vacation?

27:59.260 --> 28:01.638
Yeah, I went somewhere pretty far away.

28:02.305 --> 28:03.765
Far away? By yourself?

28:04.808 --> 28:05.892
Why did you call?

28:07.977 --> 28:09.562
I was just worried.

28:10.605 --> 28:11.689
When will you be back?

28:12.816 --> 28:15.110
What's the point?
I don't have any shows to do anyway.

28:15.193 --> 28:19.114
Still, you should stay strong
and eat well. Okay?

28:19.197 --> 28:20.490
I can handle things myself.

28:20.573 --> 28:22.409
Right. Okay.

28:35.004 --> 28:38.383
Our family isn't really
that close with each other.

28:40.593 --> 28:43.680
Your father seems worried about you.

28:44.264 --> 28:45.890
The problem is he worries too much.

28:46.808 --> 28:49.144
So, does your father…

28:49.811 --> 28:52.522
-know…
-Know about my meds?

28:53.940 --> 28:55.358
I think he does,

28:56.401 --> 28:58.027
but he doesn't mention it.

29:01.489 --> 29:03.324
How long have you been taking them?

29:05.034 --> 29:06.453
It's been…

29:07.704 --> 29:09.414
about five years.

29:09.497 --> 29:12.709
Not even a year after I joined HIT,

29:14.169 --> 29:16.671
I got the chance to host a show by myself.

29:17.714 --> 29:21.718
Something had happened
to my senior colleague.

29:25.472 --> 29:28.099
Yun-ji, are you okay?

29:28.183 --> 29:29.392
Ye-jin.

29:32.520 --> 29:34.439
I can't believe this.

29:35.482 --> 29:36.608
Ye-jin.

29:37.108 --> 29:38.193
That broadcast…

29:38.777 --> 29:40.570
-You should take it.
-What?

29:41.154 --> 29:42.906
They said I need four weeks to recover.

29:42.989 --> 29:44.199
My arm hurts.

29:46.701 --> 29:47.827
PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

29:47.911 --> 29:49.162
"Good Morning Cream"?

29:49.245 --> 29:51.247
How could I take this?

29:51.331 --> 29:53.541
The broadcast is next week.

29:53.625 --> 29:54.709
Exactly.

29:54.793 --> 29:57.295
You were helping me with it,
so you should do it.

29:58.129 --> 30:00.340
I'm not ready to be a main host yet--

30:00.423 --> 30:02.717
Song Myeong-hwa
has been confirmed as the guest.

30:03.510 --> 30:05.261
The actress Song Myeong-hwa?

30:05.762 --> 30:06.971
Yeah.

30:07.055 --> 30:09.057
I didn't want to miss the opportunity

30:09.766 --> 30:11.184
to debut as a main host.

30:12.060 --> 30:12.894
And…

30:13.812 --> 30:17.607
it was a chance to do a broadcast
with Song Myeong-hwa.

30:19.025 --> 30:21.444
But then, that incident happened.

30:21.528 --> 30:23.488
Harmful substances
were found in the cream.

30:23.571 --> 30:25.031
We demand compensation from HIT!

30:25.114 --> 30:27.450
-We demand compensation!
-We demand compensation!

30:27.534 --> 30:28.868
A GOOD CREAM? IT'S AN EVIL CREAM

30:29.828 --> 30:31.371
I'm sorry.

30:32.872 --> 30:34.249
I'm truly sorry.

30:36.084 --> 30:38.711
If I could've suffered in their stead…

30:39.712 --> 30:43.174
As of today, I shall retire

30:44.092 --> 30:45.927
from my acting career.

30:46.010 --> 30:47.470
How will you compensate the victims?

30:48.555 --> 30:51.474
If my career could've been ruined instead,
it would've been better.

30:53.893 --> 30:56.521
Mom, it's me. It's Ye-jin.

30:58.273 --> 30:59.357
Mom.

31:03.778 --> 31:04.988
Mom.

31:08.324 --> 31:09.868
I…

31:15.331 --> 31:17.041
HOST DAM YE-JIN RECEIVED HUSH MONEY

31:18.126 --> 31:20.044
I can explain everything. This is…

31:21.087 --> 31:23.256
I heard you took money from The Usu's CEO.

31:23.923 --> 31:26.551
Did you do this to get revenge?

31:26.634 --> 31:29.345
-What do you mean "revenge"?
-Are you happy now?

31:29.429 --> 31:30.763
My plan

31:30.847 --> 31:33.224
was to take all the blame for your sake.

31:34.142 --> 31:35.059
But…

31:35.935 --> 31:38.146
how could you do this to me?

31:38.229 --> 31:40.857
Mom. Just hear me out…

31:41.983 --> 31:43.026
I'm not your mom anymore.

31:48.990 --> 31:50.909
You just want to believe that, don't you?

31:52.160 --> 31:54.287
-What?
-Then, do as you wish.

31:54.370 --> 31:56.664
That seems to be
the only thing you can cling to.

31:58.124 --> 31:59.042
Are you serious?

31:59.125 --> 32:01.377
How does it feel
to have everyone turn away from you?

32:02.879 --> 32:04.088
Is it painful?

32:06.049 --> 32:08.968
I suffered every single day
after you turned away from me.

32:14.307 --> 32:16.100
You asked if I was getting revenge, right?

32:18.853 --> 32:20.396
It looks like I've succeeded.

32:27.320 --> 32:29.781
-Great work!
-Great job, everyone!

32:29.864 --> 32:31.616
You did great, Ms. Song.

32:31.699 --> 32:32.700
Honestly,

32:33.242 --> 32:34.994
I hit rock bottom.

32:38.164 --> 32:40.708
And when I could finally
get in front of the cameras again…

32:40.792 --> 32:42.919
THIS IS SEOK-GYEONG
YE-JIN'S HAVING A HARD TIME

32:43.002 --> 32:45.755
…I promised myself
I'd never make any excuses.

32:48.049 --> 32:49.801
I would do everything flawlessly

32:50.718 --> 32:53.805
without a single mistake.

32:56.432 --> 33:00.520
The time I spent on work
made everything possible.

33:02.897 --> 33:04.524
I'd review everything

33:05.274 --> 33:06.901
a hundred times instead of once.

33:11.072 --> 33:14.283
So, of course,
not even 24 hours was enough for me.

33:17.787 --> 33:19.706
I held on all those years…

33:23.001 --> 33:25.420
But I ended up having to do
another cosmetics broadcast

33:25.920 --> 33:27.672
that I'd been avoiding like the plague.

33:32.969 --> 33:35.847
To be honest, the reason why
I pestered you so much

33:37.098 --> 33:38.516
when I first came here

33:39.559 --> 33:41.894
because I was scared.

33:43.521 --> 33:44.605
I was worried

33:46.149 --> 33:48.568
that I'd miss something again.

33:50.903 --> 33:53.656
That's why I was so obsessed
with checking everything.

33:55.241 --> 33:58.870
But everything was perfect,
and that reassured me.

34:01.539 --> 34:04.292
I was able to do
another cosmetics broadcast

34:04.792 --> 34:06.794
thanks to you, Mr. Mechoori.

34:08.671 --> 34:11.591
All the moments I spent with you

34:12.967 --> 34:14.886
gave me certainty.

34:16.137 --> 34:18.848
You supported me
when even I couldn't trust myself,

34:20.433 --> 34:23.227
walked quietly by my side,

34:23.311 --> 34:24.395
and…

34:26.189 --> 34:28.399
stayed with me until the end.

34:30.401 --> 34:31.819
Thank you so much.

34:33.696 --> 34:36.115
I wanted to tell you that.

34:40.870 --> 34:42.080
That's all.

34:43.122 --> 34:44.123
The end.

34:45.458 --> 34:48.461
Thank you for listening to my long speech.

35:17.740 --> 35:18.741
We did it.

35:18.825 --> 35:21.661
-We did it!
-We did it!

35:23.704 --> 35:25.581
We did it!

35:26.749 --> 35:28.584
-Finally!
-We finally did it!

35:29.627 --> 35:31.045
We finally did it!

35:31.129 --> 35:32.130
We did it!

35:32.213 --> 35:34.006
GOOD MORNING CREAM

35:52.441 --> 35:56.070
Class President Na Som-yi,
are you all dressed yet?

35:56.946 --> 35:58.865
Hurry up and come on out.

36:00.741 --> 36:04.245
Geez, what kind of class president
is late on their first day?

36:04.328 --> 36:06.622
You should be an example
to your classmates…

36:07.957 --> 36:09.167
Jin-yi…

36:15.882 --> 36:17.508
But you know,

36:17.592 --> 36:20.469
I guess humans really are
creatures made for adapting.

36:20.553 --> 36:21.971
I used to hate having breakfast

36:22.054 --> 36:24.891
because it felt like
my stomach was filled with sand.

36:24.974 --> 36:27.018
But now, I feel empty without breakfast.

36:32.315 --> 36:33.983
There's something I need to tell you.

36:34.775 --> 36:35.776
What is it?

36:37.320 --> 36:39.071
Why do you look so serious?

36:40.948 --> 36:43.492
Mechoori! It's Som-yi!

36:43.576 --> 36:45.328
What am I going to do?

36:45.411 --> 36:46.329
What about Som-yi?

36:49.457 --> 36:50.791
Jin-yi, what's wrong with Som-yi?

36:50.875 --> 36:52.585
We have to go to the hospital.

36:52.668 --> 36:54.879
She scratched herself everywhere,
and she's bleeding.

36:58.758 --> 37:00.092
Why? How did this happen to her?

37:00.176 --> 37:01.594
Don't you dare follow us.

37:01.677 --> 37:03.512
Don't you know whose fault this is?

37:05.223 --> 37:07.642
If only I hadn't seen
your broadcast that day…

37:29.956 --> 37:33.626
USEONG HOSPITAL

37:44.262 --> 37:46.555
Som-yi, do you feel better now?

37:47.598 --> 37:48.808
I'm fine.

37:49.350 --> 37:51.143
But can't I go to school?

37:52.395 --> 37:55.231
No. You'll have to stay here for a bit
and get treated.

37:55.940 --> 37:57.733
I want to go to school though…

37:58.859 --> 38:00.820
So why did you
have to eat that stuff then?

38:01.320 --> 38:04.615
My friends wanted to eat together.
Am I the only one who should say no?

38:04.699 --> 38:06.575
That's right. You should've said no.

38:06.659 --> 38:08.286
I told you numerous times

38:08.369 --> 38:10.579
that you can't have processed foods
with eggs or flour--

38:10.663 --> 38:11.998
Okay.

38:13.541 --> 38:15.167
I'm sorry.

38:15.710 --> 38:17.336
Don't yell at me.

38:18.421 --> 38:20.423
I'm sick, Jin-yi.

38:22.091 --> 38:25.469
I'm sorry I ate burgers and fries

38:25.553 --> 38:29.765
when you told me not to.

38:44.655 --> 38:47.616
Som-yi, wait just a moment.
Don't scratch your skin.

38:58.044 --> 38:59.879
Jin-yi.

39:02.173 --> 39:04.383
I thought everything was okay now,

39:06.010 --> 39:07.553
but I was wrong.

39:07.636 --> 39:11.474
This happens to her
after eating just a single burger.

39:11.557 --> 39:13.809
I must have lost my mind!

39:19.398 --> 39:22.318
Why on earth
did you bring that woman here?

39:25.863 --> 39:28.032
I don't think I can forgive you.

39:57.478 --> 39:58.979
-Is Som-yi--
-She's been admitted.

39:59.688 --> 40:00.773
I'm sorry.

40:05.569 --> 40:07.488
If you say you're sorry,

40:08.656 --> 40:10.366
is that going to fix Som-yi's skin?

40:11.075 --> 40:13.285
I just wanted to do something

40:14.829 --> 40:17.164
until Som-yi gets better.

40:17.248 --> 40:18.082
Whatever I can do--

40:18.165 --> 40:20.167
Please, just stay out of our business.

40:21.961 --> 40:25.005
That's the only thing
you can do for Som-yi.

42:11.195 --> 42:12.696
What happened to Som-yi…

42:17.576 --> 42:19.787
was my fault.

42:21.747 --> 42:23.499
She's wearing a mask…

42:28.254 --> 42:30.464
even in this hot weather…

42:35.010 --> 42:36.679
because of me.

42:39.223 --> 42:40.641
But…

42:42.226 --> 42:44.311
even after what I'd done to her,

42:46.105 --> 42:48.732
I foolishly wanted to work again.

42:50.526 --> 42:52.528
After what I'd done to her…

42:58.492 --> 42:59.368
I…

43:00.661 --> 43:02.288
I must have lost my mind.

43:51.462 --> 43:53.631
CEO KANG MU-WON

43:56.091 --> 43:56.925
Hello?

43:57.009 --> 43:59.845
Mr. Lee, come to the office!
The numbers have exceeded the limit.

44:01.430 --> 44:02.723
GOJEUNEOK BIO

44:07.227 --> 44:09.146
Mu-won, where are the results?

44:09.229 --> 44:10.230
Here.

44:14.068 --> 44:15.110
1030 CFU/G, FAIL

44:15.194 --> 44:18.947
I felt like I was slowly falling apart
every time you checked the results,

44:19.031 --> 44:20.407
but it's finally over.

44:20.491 --> 44:23.077
Does this resolve the concern
with Ms. Dam now?

44:26.121 --> 44:27.873
What's the occasion for the call, Mr. Lee?

44:28.374 --> 44:31.377
Didn't you say you had nothing
to do with us anymore?

44:31.460 --> 44:33.629
Today's test exceeded the microbial limit.

44:37.883 --> 44:42.304
We need to bring Ms. Dam back
to where she belongs before it's too late.

44:45.432 --> 44:46.392
TEST RESULTS

44:46.475 --> 44:47.643
1030 CFU/G, FAIL

44:49.937 --> 44:52.940
Dispose of the renewal products
as soon as possible.

44:53.482 --> 44:54.316
Yes, ma'am.

45:01.198 --> 45:03.534
What about Eric?
Did he end things with HIT?

45:04.827 --> 45:07.913
He hasn't mentioned anything yet.

45:08.872 --> 45:09.957
How bothersome.

45:16.088 --> 45:17.506
-Hello?
-Hey.

45:18.132 --> 45:20.134
When are you ending things with HIT?

45:20.217 --> 45:23.971
Why are you in such a hurry?
Is there something you need to hide?

45:26.598 --> 45:29.101
So you know the numbers
have exceeded the limit.

45:30.894 --> 45:31.895
I told you.

45:32.688 --> 45:34.690
I'm in charge of the Korea launch.

45:54.376 --> 45:56.545
HIT HOMESHOPPING PROPOSAL FOR PARTNERSHIP

46:08.932 --> 46:11.226
MS. ANGRY EOM

46:14.438 --> 46:16.064
Ms. Dam, you have to see this.

46:19.485 --> 46:20.319
Hello?

46:20.402 --> 46:22.446
Are you looking at this?
Did you hear the news?

46:23.113 --> 46:25.199
-What?
-The link I sent in our group chat!

46:25.282 --> 46:27.784
-Check it right now.
-Right now!

46:35.292 --> 46:38.504
I'm Eric Seo, Executive Director
and lead of L'Étoile's Korea operations.

46:39.087 --> 46:40.547
Home shopping host Dam Ye-jin

46:40.631 --> 46:43.592
raised concerns that serious issues
could occur with our product

46:43.675 --> 46:45.385
after shipping them to customers,

46:45.469 --> 46:48.472
given the rate
at which microbial levels were increasing,

46:48.555 --> 46:51.975
and decided to change the launch
to a showcase broadcast.

46:52.059 --> 46:54.102
In the end, her decision was right.

46:54.186 --> 46:57.689
In retests carried out
by domestic and overseas labs,

46:57.773 --> 47:00.442
microbial levels
exceeding the limit were detected.

47:01.902 --> 47:05.822
We are conducting a thorough investigation
of our production factories

47:05.906 --> 47:08.784
to identify what caused
microbial levels to exceed the limit.

47:08.867 --> 47:11.620
L'Étoile will improve
our quality control system

47:11.703 --> 47:13.622
and introduce stricter safety standards

47:13.705 --> 47:17.376
to ensure that incidents like this
do not happen again.

47:17.459 --> 47:20.671
If it hadn't been for the conviction
and preemptive response

47:20.754 --> 47:22.631
of the host in charge, Dam Ye-jin,

47:22.714 --> 47:26.343
a product with safety concerns
would have been delivered to customers.

47:27.636 --> 47:29.596
To home shopping host Dam Ye-jin,

47:29.680 --> 47:34.017
for having to deal
with unfair criticism after the broadcast,

47:34.935 --> 47:37.271
and to everyone
who has trusted L'Étoile's products,

47:38.146 --> 47:42.693
once again,
we would like to sincerely apologize.

47:44.695 --> 47:45.904
Ms. Dong!

47:47.364 --> 47:50.784
Why isn't Dam Ye-jin's name
in the broadcast schedule?

47:50.867 --> 47:52.786
As you know, Dam Ye-jin--

47:52.869 --> 47:55.539
No, that was back then.
The public opinion has changed now.

47:56.123 --> 47:58.417
Right now, with her name alone,

47:58.500 --> 48:01.336
we could sell thousands of anything,
even meaningless needles.

48:01.420 --> 48:04.256
Geez, don't you have any sense
of what's going on?

48:04.339 --> 48:06.216
What are you waiting for?
Bring her back now.

48:06.300 --> 48:07.884
We have broadcasts to do.

48:07.968 --> 48:09.386
Tell her to get here immediately.

48:26.570 --> 48:27.404
Ms. Moon.

48:29.197 --> 48:31.325
Long time no see.

48:31.408 --> 48:33.702
I thought they would liven up the shop,

48:34.494 --> 48:36.163
so I brought these.

48:36.788 --> 48:38.498
-I think they'd ruin the shop.
-Okay.

48:38.582 --> 48:40.292
Then, I'll bring a potted plant next time.

48:40.375 --> 48:41.251
Ma'am.

48:41.335 --> 48:43.545
-Long time no see.
-Me?

48:45.881 --> 48:47.174
Oh, my!

48:47.257 --> 48:49.760
I can't believe my luck!

48:52.888 --> 48:54.222
-Are they real?
-Yes.

48:55.474 --> 48:58.685
I've grown more curious about you
because of your unique taste.

48:58.769 --> 49:00.312
I won't beat around the bush.

49:01.063 --> 49:02.397
What kind of man do you like?

49:03.190 --> 49:04.483
Someone who is…

49:06.234 --> 49:07.486
the exact opposite of you.

49:08.070 --> 49:10.489
Geez, he has no chance.

49:12.741 --> 49:14.993
I mean, what's wrong with me?

49:15.077 --> 49:17.996
Those corny, fancy clothes,

49:18.080 --> 49:19.748
your shoes, your hair…

49:19.831 --> 49:22.167
I hate everything from head to toe.

49:23.502 --> 49:25.003
And especially that watch.

49:26.254 --> 49:27.756
That watch

49:27.839 --> 49:30.050
makes my blood boil
just from looking at it.

49:30.550 --> 49:32.177
So get it out of my sight.

49:42.354 --> 49:43.689
A man like me…

49:45.065 --> 49:46.900
is nothing without designer brands.

49:51.530 --> 49:53.281
These precious items

49:53.782 --> 49:56.785
are what complete the man I am.

49:57.327 --> 49:58.662
Ordinary…

50:00.497 --> 50:01.623
How do I do that?

50:02.207 --> 50:04.042
Since you're ordinary,
give me some advice.

50:06.920 --> 50:08.547
Hey, are you listening to me?

50:17.305 --> 50:19.391
What is it? Is something bothering you?

50:19.474 --> 50:21.268
Ms. Dam can return to her job now.

50:21.351 --> 50:23.228
Everything went well,
so why the long face?

50:23.854 --> 50:25.147
Mu-won.

50:25.230 --> 50:27.190
I have a lot of work to do.

50:28.150 --> 50:29.192
Right.

50:38.160 --> 50:41.580
What burden is he carrying now
to make him like this?

50:59.514 --> 51:01.057
Why didn't you call me to the office?

51:01.141 --> 51:03.226
Well, we coldly kicked you out last time.

51:03.310 --> 51:05.145
Calling you back to HIT would be…

51:06.480 --> 51:07.481
a bit humiliating.

51:10.776 --> 51:12.986
You called because of the article, right?

51:13.069 --> 51:14.946
People are so funny, you know.

51:15.030 --> 51:18.033
They treat you
like an ugly duckling one day,

51:18.116 --> 51:19.951
and the next day,
they treat you like a swan.

51:25.874 --> 51:26.750
Come back to HIT.

51:27.584 --> 51:29.336
The customers are asking for you.

51:29.419 --> 51:31.505
We'll meet whatever terms you want.

51:35.884 --> 51:37.928
You must have a lot of time on your hands.

51:38.553 --> 51:40.472
You're actually hesitating?

51:40.972 --> 51:43.850
Thank you for asking me
to come back, Ms. Dong.

51:45.060 --> 51:46.144
But…

51:48.563 --> 51:50.649
right now, I need some time.

52:34.067 --> 52:35.277
Som-yi.

52:38.822 --> 52:40.031
Som-yi.

52:47.664 --> 52:49.416
Mr. Mechoori.

52:51.084 --> 52:52.085
I…

52:54.337 --> 52:56.673
I have to go to Som-yi.

53:00.510 --> 53:02.012
I have to

53:03.471 --> 53:04.890
apologize…

53:08.101 --> 53:09.311
for making her sick.

53:10.353 --> 53:11.354
Ms. Dam…

53:13.064 --> 53:14.274
Som-yi.

53:16.067 --> 53:17.402
I'm sorry.

53:19.154 --> 53:20.697
I'm sorry, Som-yi.

53:23.450 --> 53:24.367
I…

53:26.870 --> 53:28.955
I have to apologize…

53:32.334 --> 53:34.169
for making her sick.

53:52.604 --> 53:54.564
DEOKPUNG VILLAGE

54:03.698 --> 54:04.783
Come have breakfast.

54:05.492 --> 54:06.993
When did you come home?

54:07.702 --> 54:09.663
Pretty late. Take a seat.

54:27.806 --> 54:32.018
You rushed out last time
because of the microbial numbers, right?

54:33.311 --> 54:34.145
Yes.

54:35.647 --> 54:37.232
HIT reached out to me.

54:38.191 --> 54:40.860
That's great.
You can do your broadcasts now, right?

54:43.863 --> 54:45.865
You were right about what you said.

54:47.367 --> 54:51.121
You said everyone would realize
I made the right decision in the end.

54:58.545 --> 55:01.756
Make sure to come home early today
no matter what,

55:01.840 --> 55:03.633
so we can have something nice for dinner.

55:04.217 --> 55:05.218
Okay?

55:07.512 --> 55:08.388
Okay.

55:20.358 --> 55:23.111
The shareholders are furious
about the press conference.

55:24.195 --> 55:27.115
The majority of the board,
along with Ms. Michelle,

55:27.198 --> 55:29.576
are calling for you
to take responsibility.

55:31.369 --> 55:33.288
I did expect this to happen anyway.

55:34.706 --> 55:36.374
Mr. Seo.

55:36.458 --> 55:40.128
Ms. Michelle
is not going to overlook this.

55:42.672 --> 55:43.840
I'll be ready for it.

55:44.549 --> 55:45.759
I'm going to go check in then

55:45.842 --> 55:48.678
on the one person
who's on my side in Korea.

55:49.637 --> 55:52.891
I told you who I'm going to meet,
so don't follow me.

55:52.974 --> 55:55.560
Ms. Dam is turning down
all broadcast offers at the moment.

56:28.176 --> 56:31.971
I have to apologize

56:32.847 --> 56:34.974
for making her sick.

56:35.058 --> 56:36.392
I'm sorry.

56:37.936 --> 56:39.270
I'm sorry, Som-yi.

56:46.778 --> 56:47.946
Hey, Mechoori.

56:49.614 --> 56:50.698
Mechoori.

56:52.158 --> 56:53.535
By any chance,

56:53.618 --> 56:57.122
have you and Ms. Dam promised
to build a future together or something?

56:58.706 --> 57:01.459
If not, then is Ms. Dam

57:01.543 --> 57:03.545
still not feeling well?

57:05.755 --> 57:06.965
What are you trying to ask?

57:07.048 --> 57:08.258
Well…

57:11.136 --> 57:15.473
I mean, Ms. Eom
is pretty worried right now.

57:15.557 --> 57:19.769
Ms. Dam was asked to return to HIT,

57:19.853 --> 57:21.354
but she refused.

57:23.314 --> 57:25.733
Should I try contacting her?
Would that be too much?

57:26.609 --> 57:27.569
Right…

57:55.597 --> 57:56.681
Ms. Dam.

57:56.764 --> 57:58.099
Mr. Seo.

57:58.725 --> 58:02.353
Thank you for coming here.
I should've contacted you first.

58:03.271 --> 58:04.189
Right?

58:05.482 --> 58:07.192
I've prepared these as an apology.

58:07.275 --> 58:08.776
Choose whatever you like.

58:13.156 --> 58:13.990
Mr. Seo.

58:16.284 --> 58:17.410
Are you all right?

58:18.661 --> 58:20.288
You must be in a tight spot.

58:20.371 --> 58:21.623
I'm fine.

58:21.706 --> 58:24.417
I don't want you to feel troubled
by what happened.

58:24.501 --> 58:27.212
L'Étoile put you
in a difficult position first.

58:30.173 --> 58:32.759
Still, I'm really grateful.

58:33.384 --> 58:34.552
I feel much better.

58:35.678 --> 58:37.347
You really mean that, right?

58:39.390 --> 58:41.768
If it's too hard to tell me now,
you can tell me later.

58:42.519 --> 58:44.854
Just know that I'm thinking about you.

58:45.897 --> 58:48.983
Sometimes, just knowing
that someone cares about you

58:49.067 --> 58:51.236
can make you feel at ease.

59:09.128 --> 59:11.548
Mr. Lee, where are you right now?

59:15.718 --> 59:18.763
You said we had to bring her back
before it was too late.

59:18.846 --> 59:20.431
What have you been doing all this time?

59:21.391 --> 59:23.017
Just get to the point.

59:23.101 --> 59:25.603
Are you one of the reasons
why Ms. Dam refused to go back?

59:27.230 --> 59:29.482
I've put everything
on the line for Ms. Dam.

59:30.316 --> 59:32.735
But is this the best you can do for her?

59:33.319 --> 59:34.779
Think carefully

59:35.572 --> 59:37.532
about what's truly best for her.

01:00:03.391 --> 01:00:09.439
ANTIOXIDANT EFFECTS AND SKIN TONE BENEFITS
OF PEONY FLOWER EXTRACT

01:00:44.432 --> 01:00:46.351
LEE HAE-SEOK

01:00:54.192 --> 01:00:55.151
Are you that happy?

01:00:55.234 --> 01:00:56.778
I'm super happy.

01:00:56.861 --> 01:01:00.406
I got new shoes, and I made new friends.

01:01:00.490 --> 01:01:01.908
This is awesome.

01:01:03.576 --> 01:01:06.621
But why did you suddenly
want to become class president?

01:01:06.704 --> 01:01:09.082
You didn't want kids looking at you
so you'd skip school.

01:01:09.165 --> 01:01:14.504
I thought everyone was staring at my mask,
so I just wanted to hide all the time.

01:01:15.129 --> 01:01:16.464
But like Coach said,

01:01:16.547 --> 01:01:19.258
I wasn't bothered by it,
so they weren't bothered either.

01:01:19.342 --> 01:01:24.180
When I stood tall and made eye contact
as I spoke, it was no big deal.

01:01:24.764 --> 01:01:27.475
"Coach"? Who are you talking about?

01:01:32.480 --> 01:01:34.357
I heard you helped Som-yi.

01:01:36.192 --> 01:01:38.194
She's become a lot more cheerful.

01:01:39.278 --> 01:01:41.906
And I just found out it was thanks to you.

01:01:43.491 --> 01:01:45.243
In my head, I know it.

01:01:45.326 --> 01:01:47.620
You wouldn't have knowingly sold them.

01:01:48.496 --> 01:01:49.914
But I can't…

01:01:51.332 --> 01:01:54.252
But I can't forget the words you said
on your broadcast that day.

01:01:56.170 --> 01:01:58.589
You said it with that face and voice

01:01:59.841 --> 01:02:01.217
that it was safe to buy.

01:02:01.718 --> 01:02:03.720
Our Good Morning Cream

01:02:03.803 --> 01:02:05.513
is safe for sensitive skin

01:02:05.596 --> 01:02:08.641
and even infants and children
can use it without worry.

01:02:08.725 --> 01:02:11.060
"Can use it without worry."

01:02:11.144 --> 01:02:12.478
The cream for your entire family.

01:02:12.562 --> 01:02:13.479
Som-yi could use this.

01:02:13.563 --> 01:02:15.648
Try it out today.

01:02:17.734 --> 01:02:19.110
I saw the news.

01:02:19.736 --> 01:02:21.946
There's no reason to stay here
any longer, right?

01:02:24.490 --> 01:02:27.076
I'm already overwhelmed
with taking care of Som-yi.

01:02:28.327 --> 01:02:30.663
I don't want to waste energy
hating anyone.

01:02:31.330 --> 01:02:32.832
For our sake at least,

01:02:34.459 --> 01:02:36.210
I'd like you to go back now.

01:02:58.357 --> 01:02:59.776
You're home early.

01:03:13.873 --> 01:03:14.749
Ms. Dam.

01:03:16.834 --> 01:03:18.878
I have something to tell you.

01:03:18.961 --> 01:03:21.589
I heard you turned down
the reinstatement offer.

01:03:23.508 --> 01:03:25.718
I don't think I can return at the moment.

01:03:26.427 --> 01:03:27.720
Because of Som-yi?

01:03:31.307 --> 01:03:32.558
Doesn't it feel unfair?

01:03:34.519 --> 01:03:36.103
What happened to Som-yi,

01:03:37.146 --> 01:03:38.773
technically, wasn't your fault.

01:03:40.274 --> 01:03:42.610
It was because of the person
who made that awful cream.

01:03:43.236 --> 01:03:44.987
I don't want to blame others for it.

01:03:45.071 --> 01:03:46.781
I made it.

01:03:46.864 --> 01:03:48.366
The Good Morning Cream.

01:03:52.161 --> 01:03:54.789
I'm the one who made that awful cream.

01:04:17.353 --> 01:04:18.187
I know.

01:04:20.106 --> 01:04:21.983
Then there's no need to explain further.

01:04:22.984 --> 01:04:25.736
You should head back now
to where you once were.

01:04:27.613 --> 01:04:29.824
Is that all you have to say to me?

01:04:32.118 --> 01:04:33.995
That can't be the end of it.

01:04:35.371 --> 01:04:36.873
Don't you have anything else to say?

01:04:37.999 --> 01:04:39.333
What do you want me to say?

01:04:39.417 --> 01:04:41.836
You couldn't tell me until now

01:04:42.712 --> 01:04:44.797
because there was a reason, right?

01:04:45.882 --> 01:04:48.092
It's okay, so tell me.

01:04:48.175 --> 01:04:49.510
No, I have to hear it.

01:04:49.594 --> 01:04:50.928
I'm done talking.

01:04:52.722 --> 01:04:54.807
Why did you bring me here then?

01:04:57.393 --> 01:05:01.022
Were you planning to just end things
whenever you felt like it?

01:05:06.569 --> 01:05:08.112
I saw that you were still suffering

01:05:08.905 --> 01:05:10.781
because of the cream I made.

01:05:10.865 --> 01:05:12.408
I felt guilty. That's why.

01:05:14.952 --> 01:05:16.579
I thought I'd feel better

01:05:16.662 --> 01:05:18.497
if I took care of you

01:05:19.290 --> 01:05:21.125
until you got better.

01:05:23.878 --> 01:05:24.712
You're lying.

01:05:24.795 --> 01:05:25.796
But…

01:05:26.964 --> 01:05:28.174
it's no use.

01:05:29.592 --> 01:05:31.344
Just take your stuff and leave.

01:05:32.094 --> 01:05:34.055
I know you're lying.

01:05:36.057 --> 01:05:38.935
All that time we spent together
couldn't have…

01:05:39.685 --> 01:05:41.103
It's suffocating.

01:05:45.107 --> 01:05:47.443
I feel suffocated when I'm with you.

01:05:56.118 --> 01:05:58.120
SOLD OUT ON YOU

01:06:31.237 --> 01:06:32.738
Mechoori! What's up with you?

01:06:32.822 --> 01:06:34.031
This isn't like you at all.

01:06:34.115 --> 01:06:36.450
-Just stop. Live your own life.
-It's the least I can do.

01:06:36.534 --> 01:06:39.036
Am I the kind of person
people get tired of?

01:06:39.120 --> 01:06:40.579
Everyone leaves if I show them love.

01:06:40.663 --> 01:06:43.249
Couldn't you try
reaching out to Ye-jin first?

01:06:43.332 --> 01:06:45.793
Why do you hate
Dam Ye-jin so much, Ms. Ji?

01:06:47.753 --> 01:06:50.256
-Mr. Seo?
-Ms. Dam. You live here?

01:06:50.881 --> 01:06:54.468
All our clients are suddenly canceling
their contracts as if it was coordinated.

01:06:54.552 --> 01:06:55.469
We haven't met before.

01:06:55.553 --> 01:06:57.054
You should be happy to see me.

01:06:57.138 --> 01:06:58.889
This is the last option for Gojeuneok.

01:07:00.266 --> 01:07:02.184
I still have more to say to you.

01:07:02.268 --> 01:07:04.478
Let's meet up and end things properly.

01:07:10.943 --> 01:07:12.945
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park
